00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.280 align:start position:0%
at least 60 people are reported dead in  wildfires raging outside of the capital  of Greece a pair of large fires is  burning in coastal areas near Athens  some tourists and residents were forced  to flee to the beach for safety rescue  crews from across Europe are racing to  Greece to help gale force winds and dry  conditions are fueling these flames this  is the deadliest fire season to hit  Greece in more than a decade Seth Doane  has the latest  good morning Greece's issued an urgent  appeal for help in battling the worst  fires they've seen there since 2007 a  wildfire tore through a beach resort  community popular with tourists and  retirees the Coast Guard and passing  boats reported picking up around 700  people who had fled to beaches for  safety but tragically the fire swept  through too quickly for others to save  themselves and in some cases families  reportedly trapped behind a wall of fire  and smoke rescue crews reported finding  more than 20 people huddled together on  a beach and the Red Cross told local  media that some had apparently been  family members who were found hugging  each other the fire was ignited on  Monday but winds died down a bit today  offering some relief but the fire is not  yet under control for CBS this morning  Seth Doane Rob
 

